        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Define target segments, outreach cadence, and prospect list priorities.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 46183,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, let's start thinking about T4. Before I build out the full prospect list in A4, I wanted to propose a few initial customer segments to target. Based on past purchases, I think we should focus on:\n1. Customers who bought premium products in the last 6 months.\n2. Clients with expiring service contracts.\nWhat are your thoughts?",
            "mentions": [
              31942,
              52934,
              54019,
              488135
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 52934,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "I like both of those. Expiring contracts are a perfect trigger. I'd add a third: customers who have contacted support more than 3 times in the last year. They're engaged and likely see value in priority support. For T5, I can draft an outreach cadence (A6) based on these segments.",
            "mentions": [
              46183
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 54019,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Those three segments sound good. How will we prioritize between them for the first couple of weeks?",
